    - target: {fileID: 4586130411077341659, guid: 86034297a83190f49ab0adafb47440cb,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Size
      value: 0.4207692
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4586130411077341659, guid: 86034297a83190f49ab0adafb47440cb,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Value
      value: 1.0000017
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 5336956100140916112, guid: 86034297a83190f49ab0adafb47440cb,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Modern UIs provides multiple ways to add or remove players from whitelists
        in-game. These tools are useful for granting temporary access to systems,
        managing event permissions, or assigning roles directly in the world.\n\nWhitelist
        editors are not whitelists themselves. Instead, they interact with whitelists
        that implement the Whitelist Setter Base, meaning they can work with both
        local and synced whitelists.\n\nAccess to whitelist editors can also be restricted
        using another whitelist (e.g. a String Load), allowing you to control who
        is permitted to manage permissions.\n\nAll editor types are available as
        either standalone components or Main UI Elements.\n\n<b>Basic Buttons, Inputs
        & Zones</b>\n\n<b>Add To / Remove From Whitelist Input Field</b>\n\u2022
        Allows manually entering a player's display name\n\u2022 Can add or remove
        players from a whitelist\n\n<b>Add All / Remove All Button</b>\n\u2022 Adds
        all players currently in the instance to a whitelist\n\u2022 Can also completely
        clear a whitelist\n\n<b>Auto Add To Whitelist</b>\n\u2022 Automatically adds
        all current players to a whitelist\n\u2022 Continues to add newly joined
        players while enabled\n\n<b>Whitelist Zone Add</b>\n\u2022 Automatically
        adds players inside a trigger zone to a whitelist\n\u2022 Useful for tracking
        who is in a specific area\n\n<b>Editors & Requestors</b>\n\n<b>Whitelist
        Editor</b>\n\u2022 Displays players currently in the instance\n\u2022 Allows
        adding players to a whitelist with a button press\n\u2022 Supports removing
        players who are already whitelisted\n\n<b>Whitelist Requestor</b>\n\u2022
        Allows players to request access to a whitelist\n\u2022 Requests can be approved
        or denied by authorized users\n\u2022 Useful for self-service permission
        systems and event access requests for e.g. DJs\n\n<b>Persistence</b>\n\nWhitelist
        Persistence allows the current state of a whitelist to be saved between instances.\n\nWhen
        a new instance is created, the saved data will automatically be restored
        if you are the first player to join the instance. This makes it possible
        to carry over permissions, access lists, and other whitelist data without
        needing to reconfigure them each time a new instance is created."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 5757065297534502311, guid: 86034297a83190f49ab0adafb47440cb,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Info
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
